1
00:00:00,122 --> 00:00:02,563
I traced those numbers to where they actually live:

2
00:00:02,603 --> 00:00:03,185
in a ledger.

3
00:00:03,225 --> 00:00:05,071
Kept by an entity called the bank.

4
00:00:05,111 --> 00:00:08,493
When Alice pays Bob thirty dollars, nothing moves.

5
00:00:08,533 --> 00:00:10,278
The bank erases a number here,

6
00:00:10,318 --> 00:00:13,264
writes one there. Your salary: a number. Your rent:

7
00:00:13,304 --> 00:00:13,880
a number.

8
00:00:13,920 --> 00:00:15,986
You have never actually seen this money.

9
00:00:16,026 --> 00:00:17,731
Every bank keeps its own ledger.

10
00:00:17,771 --> 00:00:19,414
So every night they check each other's.

11
00:00:19,454 --> 00:00:21,009
Because none of them trusts the others.

12
00:00:21,049 --> 00:00:23,043
So a bank is not a vault full of money.

13
00:00:23,083 --> 00:00:24,291
A bank is a ledger.

14
00:00:24,331 --> 00:00:26,491
And whoever holds the ledger holds everything.

15
00:00:26,531 --> 00:00:28,378
The ledger holder can charge a fee,

16
00:00:28,418 --> 00:00:30,181
delay you, freeze your account,

17
00:00:30,221 --> 00:00:32,307
or go bankrupt with your money.

18
00:00:32,347 --> 00:00:33,580
This is not a theory.

19
00:00:33,620 --> 00:00:34,519
On the island of Cyprus,

20
00:00:34,559 --> 00:00:37,398
in 2013, people woke up to find the banks closed.

21
00:00:37,438 --> 00:00:39,197
Anyone with over a hundred thousand euros in the

22
00:00:39,237 --> 00:00:41,463
biggest bank lost almost half the excess.

23
00:00:41,503 --> 00:00:42,627
To rescue the bank.

24
00:00:42,667 --> 00:00:44,966
But what if that ledger didn't belong to anyone

25
00:00:45,006 --> 00:00:45,852
at all?

26
00:00:45,892 --> 00:00:47,807
That's the idea that changed everything.

27
00:00:48,054 --> 00:00:50,246
The full report is on the Earth Report channel.

28
00:00:50,286 --> 00:00:52,054
Subscribe to the channel and turn on the bell

29
00:00:52,094 --> 00:00:54,683
so my secret reports on your planet reach you first.
